a55f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-64656" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\pi $ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\pi $:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\text{ }\\frac{1}{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "8387ce10-0bc1-5ffe-a591-855b4ae20824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "b752ef19-fb1c-51d4-a3d8-52736da8ac80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e6f17cab-a60f-5a34-b63f-bf1da75f6491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "eec64b32-6ab6-5d2b-8327-40021fcf9f26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "29d47cde-589d-5437-8d6e-ef37f8f02e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33aba8fd-9eca-5799-b6cd-e5ccf77a6c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83661/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-83661/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-83661/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-83661/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-83661/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" "q-83661/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83661" :question/id #uuid "671565b5-8123-5c62-806e-29b6e861d216" :question/math-academy-id "q-83661" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\pi $ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83661/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bed8ef54-a7e1-5e04-8e42-81532763479e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "ee238e59-2d7e-581d-a892-7de91e846aa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "57809b3e-73fe-5eb6-aa45-b3375b57ae61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "35b62871-2426-5d76-a966-370a9960dedc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "3c63ddec-a0bf-5108-980f-17759a597dc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c2a918-7d29-596f-9f34-3fc95c65c6af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83660/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-83660/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-83660/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-83660/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-83660/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-83660/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83660" :question/id #uuid "b679e87b-7726-5f56-8563-4104ba1cd1f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-83660" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\frac{1}{4}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n \n\n$$\nT(s)=-\\sqrt{1-2s}\\,i+\\sqrt{2s}\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\sqrt{1-2s})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2s})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{-2}{2\\sqrt{1-2s}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{2s}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2s}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s}}\\,j \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{1}{4}) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2(\\frac{1}{4})}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(\\frac{1}{4})}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{1}{4}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{1}{4})‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83660/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "77b01aa7-c7eb-50c8-97c6-9d73130df290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278/selection/2faeea9c9eedefeae671c807b51ede422449e2976700bcbd604b58e50a79be38" :answer/id #uuid "e4b367c8-8913-599d-b565-b95f92cee7c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278/selection/b546c29e3eb561fca09ed32f3598ddb3cf90f00da3e078327b5c9bab102a6bda" :answer/id #uuid "a67a6afa-31e0-5aca-9d22-62948b77d967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "387c1d81-aad6-5dd3-adc7-f703173a6916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278/selection/4e28bc8958657ac76479873678314aec898957b5db14c19cd0c35563c3140cfb" :answer/id #uuid "4a38e0d3-5e2d-5953-969d-1d3f6ab36013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "22584bd6-af91-51f7-aa49-0f48c9decdda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34278/selection/b546c29e3eb561fca09ed32f3598ddb3cf90f00da3e078327b5c9bab102a6bda" :answer-field/choices ["q-34278/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-34278/selection/2faeea9c9eedefeae671c807b51ede422449e2976700bcbd604b58e50a79be38" "q-34278/selection/b546c29e3eb561fca09ed32f3598ddb3cf90f00da3e078327b5c9bab102a6bda" "q-34278/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-34278/selection/4e28bc8958657ac76479873678314aec898957b5db14c19cd0c35563c3140cfb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-34278" :question/id #uuid "40d38b64-215d-5bc3-b1ab-04d8eb937bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-34278" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=5\\pi $, if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n \n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=5\\pi $: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{5})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))\\,k \\\\  & =(0)\\,i-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(5\\pi ) & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\cdot (5\\pi )}{5})\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\cdot (5\\pi )}{5})\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (-1)\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (0)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(5\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(5\\pi )‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-34278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "76b06026-6465-5f09-ad30-d77e8e12e88d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "42d5def5-944b-5ff3-952c-f0c525e3fb1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "31d4dc9d-36da-5aa7-bc16-be4f461b16db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0fedd8b2-1a51-53d7-a72c-f9c6bd3abf48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "75c555e7-d755-5f23-a7de-e6a7211c1958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8bdfc6d-3bd0-5a18-9e9f-e7ee9e5ac5dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80607/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-80607/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-80607/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-80607/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-80607/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-80607/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80607" :question/id #uuid "86a47b66-de80-5638-9fcc-a1a0a4f55dcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-80607" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=1$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}}⟨1,s⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}}⟨1,s⟩) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{s}{(1+{s}^{2})^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{1}{(1+{s}^{2})^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{s}^{2})^{3/2}}⟨-s,1⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{(1+{1}^{2})^{3/2}}⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}‖⟨-1,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9befd973-a2d9-567a-8808-d126ecaaae1b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "2e5d7158-3001-5492-badf-5929455b3192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "b985eddf-a72a-5057-9a0b-2cadf1550c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "04054456-0d8e-58a6-b3b4-2ccad654979c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "9d550b3a-83df-5437-9f82-06df0464b57e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "78a41b1b-b1f7-589d-9ced-09467caa8347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06b973f3-1c9f-5fcf-80c0-70a73c4ac8fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131938/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-131938/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-131938/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-131938/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-131938/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" "q-131938/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131938" :question/id #uuid "04cb0eab-4d51-5c82-ab5e-f82970468540" :question/math-academy-id "q-131938" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le \\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩ \\\\  & =-3⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-3|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡3s+{sin}^{2}⁡3s} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131938/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131938"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "8e6aa1de-cba2-58a8-beee-d4df003deb77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "cabc72c7-dfd1-583c-8d36-efdb93dd4f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "dfbc3c51-1585-56c8-ad1d-4067b4e715dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "1a268556-678c-54ba-a33d-9faf0be9a7df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "95dd5850-7234-5f16-a88d-6d8c8772882a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d143e93-4052-569a-a682-3bc5ec94b44b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131931/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-131931/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-131931/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-131931/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-131931/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-131931/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131931" :question/id #uuid "d9627eb7-f5cb-5971-9464-539378dd4816" :question/math-academy-id "q-131931" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3}⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le 4\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131931/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e69a0b39-43b3-5498-a6bd-e696497105b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "cbbb71a1-ea4d-5cac-a185-a83042e6bbb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" :answer/id #uuid "cf7f8141-5d33-5f33-a8dc-a0eee2dd8fef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "95d96a3f-16b6-5885-9bf3-6dcb2f9e9772" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523/selection/ed2291aaa5801bdfea85bb6eaebc5df39c902d1e03ab1a86b6d27ed9dde3c019" :answer/id #uuid "48d7d67d-021a-5646-878e-b6d76737adb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7b2f181-6ba2-5c17-8b94-d909a5baf880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80523/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-80523/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-80523/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-80523/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" "q-80523/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-80523/selection/ed2291aaa5801bdfea85bb6eaebc5df39c902d1e03ab1a86b6d27ed9dde3c019"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80523" :question/id #uuid "81c43925-af96-58c6-a9d2-93a85250f5ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-80523" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩,\\,0\\le s<10\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{5}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80523/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80523"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "134d8e18-6b80-5ab9-8da3-c4c3a7c5f4f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559/selection/19bc88a913a5158265f131995021b969f4482ff5f6da1df562115a338bd4edd6" :answer/id #uuid "87ca4763-4f16-5966-b14a-7bb612ea531f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{s}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "357a53a6-4c35-520b-9fce-e4715a9a1588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559/selection/6eebd57dee4b7df98565b4c1ce055c4b4eac4c98eed9ab95665e2a2e0338b6db" :answer/id #uuid "633c1b15-7374-5426-a128-9b261097d5a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559/selection/06cd44af366a30d6c5aa3d8a0e3fa0f0f59b1338fff6e7d4e7b5f5aac7d8e48e" :answer/id #uuid "0677aa1e-88a0-53c6-a935-f51fc753deab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "de461b81-f17f-5a5f-a6bd-e8be08c4b1aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132559/selection/06cd44af366a30d6c5aa3d8a0e3fa0f0f59b1338fff6e7d4e7b5f5aac7d8e48e" :answer-field/choices ["q-132559/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-132559/selection/19bc88a913a5158265f131995021b969f4482ff5f6da1df562115a338bd4edd6" "q-132559/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-132559/selection/6eebd57dee4b7df98565b4c1ce055c4b4eac4c98eed9ab95665e2a2e0338b6db" "q-132559/selection/06cd44af366a30d6c5aa3d8a0e3fa0f0f59b1338fff6e7d4e7b5f5aac7d8e48e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132559" :question/id #uuid "33f2de71-7251-5165-b101-a9ebdce74546" :question/math-academy-id "q-132559" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨s-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡s,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({s}^{2}+1)⟩,\\,s\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({s}^{2}+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4s}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{2(1-{s}^{2})}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟨4s,\\,2(1-{s}^{2})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(4s)^{2}+{(2(1-{s}^{2}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{s}^{2}+4{s}^{4}-8{s}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{4{s}^{4}+8{s}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{4({s}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+1)}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545/selection/52e9e8dea39afc4471355191da8eb2ac60ff9df46ec7b57afffa59241cbc0d42" :answer/id #uuid "111253d6-597b-5177-a512-1e6803d1deb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545/selection/dfd459f2e933bdbee4a751226646ad7e8481223f81bf612b5a307585af797c66" :answer/id #uuid "2e9dfd7b-1276-5189-8c70-e2b9aa65314d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545/selection/004aadcb594c4b7adc597d3fac102bb1e63418e5c1b91fd1be195a8f88e2cde5" :answer/id #uuid "4e22e866-42c3-5db5-bd40-6d83839779dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545/selection/2fdbb2fadcd75b3c45e505d837bc929462acd6b0c55cd37974fcf263124982dd" :answer/id #uuid "8258e17d-f450-5182-9356-c1596555c733" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2s}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "51088d10-8f4c-5768-ad9a-3791a3cb40ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d5c55f6-a8b6-5b1b-9e9a-564b9225a6cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80545/selection/52e9e8dea39afc4471355191da8eb2ac60ff9df46ec7b57afffa59241cbc0d42" :answer-field/choices ["q-80545/selection/52e9e8dea39afc4471355191da8eb2ac60ff9df46ec7b57afffa59241cbc0d42" "q-80545/selection/dfd459f2e933bdbee4a751226646ad7e8481223f81bf612b5a307585af797c66" "q-80545/selection/004aadcb594c4b7adc597d3fac102bb1e63418e5c1b91fd1be195a8f88e2cde5" "q-80545/selection/2fdbb2fadcd75b3c45e505d837bc929462acd6b0c55cd37974fcf263124982dd" "q-80545/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80545" :question/id #uuid "c2bbdf17-a220-5afb-81ff-e40c2d80e604" :question/math-academy-id "q-80545" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s,$ where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{1}{3}(1-2s)^{3/2},\\,\\frac{1}{3}(2s)^{3/2}⟩,\\,0<s<\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{3}(1-2s)^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{3}(2s)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (1-2s)^{1/2}\\cdot (-2),\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (2s)^{1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-(1-2s)^{1/2},\\,(2s)^{1/2}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-(1-2s)^{1/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}((2s)^{1/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-2s)^{-1/2}\\cdot (-2),\\,\\frac{1}{2}(2s)^{-1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(1-2s)^{-1/2},\\,(2s)^{-1/2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, the curvature is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{((1-2s)^{-1/2})}^{2}+{((2s)^{-1/2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-2s)^{-1}+(2s)^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-2s}+\\frac{1}{2s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80545/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665/selection/fa91d56d78868e9d45ba7c7bcb6ea7f03a7905111c76255fd87977749acae07f" :answer/id #uuid "7503fe00-cbb9-5015-9fcc-29253f463f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665/selection/94a2eff28e864cda7d462d2bbd71e2b64dfd54838eac217703ed2d06fecff6d1" :answer/id #uuid "1e91e928-fc3b-55e1-8c86-5c6ce2dc36a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665/selection/a14260ce38a19f5a66fedf7e5cea9530720217ad79736cbc5550161d98d94cfd" :answer/id #uuid "0f09243a-4849-55a2-9778-a1a79b250ad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665/selection/273e29941f89216dab2987077631afaf2c41f226b8a40dea69fa990aa1b49c36" :answer/id #uuid "b072038c-1b78-5369-9604-705bc73eae8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665/selection/3d9aa7200b0b6e3aff078809851e350961aaa6c2ff508465f202ef1b3b6348f5" :answer/id #uuid "b1355134-f573-5898-8050-3988459eef20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a285d2b-c3a3-50ff-b767-87c82d5357d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83665/selection/fa91d56d78868e9d45ba7c7bcb6ea7f03a7905111c76255fd87977749acae07f" :answer-field/choices ["q-83665/selection/fa91d56d78868e9d45ba7c7bcb6ea7f03a7905111c76255fd87977749acae07f" "q-83665/selection/94a2eff28e864cda7d462d2bbd71e2b64dfd54838eac217703ed2d06fecff6d1" "q-83665/selection/a14260ce38a19f5a66fedf7e5cea9530720217ad79736cbc5550161d98d94cfd" "q-83665/selection/273e29941f89216dab2987077631afaf2c41f226b8a40dea69fa990aa1b49c36" "q-83665/selection/3d9aa7200b0b6e3aff078809851e350961aaa6c2ff508465f202ef1b3b6348f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83665" :question/id #uuid "cc02cdb1-2d7d-5481-92b3-bd104f553197" :question/math-academy-id "q-83665" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨1,\\,t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{t}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{t}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}+\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83665/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83665"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "59769bf3-e14c-5396-950c-a17a351c4261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "017a4c53-dd08-518d-b3c1-4a67e5747ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "729bd64a-ea77-5491-bbc1-b7ded65b0afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "63cfad54-7e47-5ea5-b175-49268cbac3e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "b627e214-548d-5c30-b76b-605d449f6a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddfd5e10-2777-5326-a513-6b9083154974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64661/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-64661/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-64661/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-64661/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-64661/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-64661/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64661" :question/id #uuid "879ff44d-4ae9-53d3-be05-23291145ff73" :question/math-academy-id "q-64661" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+2\\,j-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64661/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "40f796a6-9577-53ce-8d7a-623db79978f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e009a08f-cf6f-50c8-9c32-45c28b012bd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5a6ba93f-dbd2-54a9-bd32-37ff7dc5ea87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "828d02bc-82dc-5a9d-ab0c-0a03aa9cead6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "1c4a2212-b70b-5e2f-8605-65d560570169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c76a2ed-f3b4-55cb-8dfd-56aa5060dc1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80614/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-80614/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-80614/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-80614/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-80614/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-80614/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80614" :question/id #uuid "7a552a20-b68a-5458-863f-bfcbe95a1e07" :question/math-academy-id "q-80614" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\,i-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\,j,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{2\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4-{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{t}{2\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4(4-{t}^{2})}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}+4-{t}^{2}}{4(4-{t}^{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}{(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80614/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80614"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4fe837e9-bfd9-5cd2-93a8-719b7ab46590" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "df54df4a-2176-5738-ab88-221896135aad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "76a9a6f5-238c-52a1-9b9f-af5226b21281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "aceb664d-d2eb-572c-8211-67c8c2839a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "61949ca0-bb39-55a5-a7fe-609458aaf6e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c6861ba-8c63-597c-9aea-1e769b4f36ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64666/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-64666/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-64666/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-64666/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-64666/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-64666/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64666" :question/id #uuid "0c85d7fd-dc8f-5b1c-8a4d-1fe80acb12a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-64666" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2})}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64666/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230/selection/f13559641354da9e3e251808f99dc206efcbf80475df3c89ebf092a3f934a61e" :answer/id #uuid "0c9aa9d8-ec0b-577e-852f-2d238ecdd5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230/selection/2989de416bd2808dcbe0cdd898281156774489bb6b8c458ff1e2de131c4fb4e6" :answer/id #uuid "f4a86e4d-9b32-5a1e-905e-27a472c6d799" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230/selection/7cecf085deb70108d385fd8174c2bda391af73d6dff8b34994e3789b693c52fe" :answer/id #uuid "85dd906f-690c-5a0a-844e-23aa85fe37d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6t}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230/selection/d9af39800fd167f566a4ad913598bf34984b41cbb142328537cc221c54a63955" :answer/id #uuid "b2d00f59-5e08-5871-a577-0bb0fd1fe356" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230/selection/9ee70f3b358fc1688533f548d7847f9562fc3983cecc8a70af2ae4839db35670" :answer/id #uuid "e1c2725f-6378-5866-96c3-b1a685dbfefa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3t}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9be4fc6-b0a6-5ff3-aac6-81243d4b9d87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131230/selection/f13559641354da9e3e251808f99dc206efcbf80475df3c89ebf092a3f934a61e" :answer-field/choices ["q-131230/selection/f13559641354da9e3e251808f99dc206efcbf80475df3c89ebf092a3f934a61e" "q-131230/selection/2989de416bd2808dcbe0cdd898281156774489bb6b8c458ff1e2de131c4fb4e6" "q-131230/selection/7cecf085deb70108d385fd8174c2bda391af73d6dff8b34994e3789b693c52fe" "q-131230/selection/d9af39800fd167f566a4ad913598bf34984b41cbb142328537cc221c54a63955" "q-131230/selection/9ee70f3b358fc1688533f548d7847f9562fc3983cecc8a70af2ae4839db35670"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131230" :question/id #uuid "411461d6-184e-5c4a-888b-610d1e8adfdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-131230" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point $t>0$ on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨2t,\\,-3{t}^{2}⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}⟨3t,\\,2⟩,\\,t\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(3t)}^{2}+{(2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{9{t}^{2}+4} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+{(-3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6}{9{t}^{2}+4})}{t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131230/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c9d719f-4936-5994-90eb-c33da57639cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131230"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3135"] :question/problem "Consider the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = -\\dfrac{4}{5}\\sin{s}\\,\\mathbf i+\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sin{s}\\, \\mathbf j + \\cos{s}\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(s)$ are both parametrized by the arc length $s,$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $\\mathbf T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)k \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+0\\,j-k \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖=‖-k‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3141"] :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(s) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s , \\: -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s, \\: \\sin s \\right\\rangle,\n\\quad 0\\leq s \\lt 2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\mathbf T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s,$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\| = \\| \\mathbf{r}''(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(s)$ and $\\mathbf r''(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3140"] :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(t) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin t, \\:2\\cos t \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $\\mathbf T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf \\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\left\\| \\mathbf T'(t) \\right\\|}{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\|}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
